Clean up orphaned GroupUserProfile nodes, without double-deleting them.

Two places left orphaned GroupUserProfile nodes (a group-membership join
node with no group pointing back at it) around, breaking the group-edit
UI's profile display:

1. Deleting an account didn't clean up that account's GroupUserProfile
   nodes in other groups.
2. (Originally) removing a user from a group via GroupDAO.update also
   didn't clean up the now-detached GroupUserProfile node.

For (2): GroupModel.userProfiles is declared cascadeDelete=true,
autoUpdate=true upstream (both 1.5.0 and 1.5.4), so sparql.update(group)
already deletes a removed user's GroupUserProfileModel as part of the same
call -- a separate manual delete of the same URI right after throws
NotFoundURIException ("URI not found : ..."), even though the removal
itself already succeeded. Guard the manual cleanup with a
try/catch(NotFoundURIException) so it's a no-op when cascadeDelete beat it
to it, instead of surfacing an error to the group-edit screen.

--- a/opensilex-security/src/main/java/org/opensilex/security/group/dal/GroupDAO.java
+++ b/opensilex-security/src/main/java/org/opensilex/security/group/dal/GroupDAO.java
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
